<<<
plain makes plainness. P. sailing is (‘ probably "—OED) a popular use of the nautical term plane sailing, which means navigation by a plane chart, ‘a simple & easy method, approximately correct for short distances’.
===
**plain** makes *plainness*. *P. sailing* is ('probably'—OED) a popular use of the nautical term *plane sailing*, which means navigation by a plane chart, 'a simple & easy method, approximately correct for short distances'.
>>>

<<<
The corruption, if it is one, is so little misleading, since plain sailing is as intelligible in itself as clear going or any such phrase, that any attempt to correct it is needless as well as vain.
===
The corruption, if it is one, is so little misleading, since *plain sailing* is as intelligible in itself as *clear going* or any such phrase, that any attempt to correct it is needless as well as vain.
>>>

